    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0625" n="1359" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1359"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 698.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that it is
                    deemed most prudent to delay making a formal demand for payment of loss
                    sustained by the burning of missionary property at Harpoot and Marash until a
                    full statement of the amount of damages sustained is made and your answer to
                    this dispatch by telegram is received. It is not probable that the amount of
                    actual values destroyed will be known here before this reaches you. * * *</p>
                <p>It is hoped that facts showing values destroyed will be fully known when this has
                    reached you, and before acting I will await your telegraphic instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
